IMPORT prelude

-- Roman Catholic Archbishop Act 1975 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "The Titular Roman Catholic Archbishop of Singapore" is, and
-- who stands in during a vacancy (s 2(1), (3)); what it may do (s 2(1), (2)); the bar on concurrent office-holders and the end of a
-- power of attorney (s 2(4)); which property it took over from the Titular Roman Catholic Bishop of Malacca (s 3); how its deeds are
-- validly sealed and signed (s 4); what a Gazette notification proves (s 5); whose rights the Act leaves alone (s 6); and how the
-- former Corporation's agreements, staff, unfinished business and liabilities carry over (s 7).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RCAA1975.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The body carries
-- no amendment annotation. The legislative history lists Act 42 of 1975, commenced 12 December 1975, and the 1985 Revised Edition
-- (Chapter 375); the comparative table says only that s 2(3) and (4) of the 2020 Edition were s 2(3) of the 1985 Edition.
-- The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is one line out of step with the body; this row follows the body's numbers.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0246 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance (historical, private and spent Acts). It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario
-- has asked a sharper question yet. The Act has seven sections, so all of them except the short title are in scope. For a person
-- outside the Church it matters when buying from, leasing from, lending to or suing the Corporation (ss 2, 4, 5), for title to
-- property once held by the Bishop of Malacca (s 3), and for anyone who contracted with or worked for the former Corporation (s 7).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the preamble's history except as background; the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of
-- Property Act 1886, to which s 4(1) refers (whether a power of attorney was "deposited" under it is taken as a stated fact); what
-- "the respective estates and interests" in s 3 are; how a pension or gratuity is computed under s 7(2) (the Act says only that
-- service is continuous); the Corporation's internal governance, about which the Act says nothing.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Roman Catholic Archbishop Act 1975 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2(1), 2(3) and 5 -- who is the Corporation, and what the Gazette proves`

-- s 2(1): "The Right Reverend Michael Olcomendy, the Titular Roman Catholic Archbishop of Singapore and his successors in office shall
-- be a body corporate (referred to in this Act as the Corporation)" named "The Titular Roman Catholic Archbishop of Singapore", with
-- perpetual succession and a corporate seal.
-- s 2(3): "'Successors in office' shall be deemed to include either an Administrator Apostolic or a Vicar Capitular administering the
-- affairs of the Archdiocese of Singapore in Singapore from the time when the office ... becomes vacant by the resignation or death of
-- the holder for the time being or vacant for any other reason until the formal assumption of office by his successor."
-- s 5: a Gazette notification of the appointment of any person to exercise the office of Archbishop, or of Administrator Apostolic or
-- Vicar Capitular, "shall be conclusive evidence that such person was duly authorised to exercise that office in Singapore".
--
-- An Administrator Apostolic or Vicar Capitular is a successor in office only while the Archbishopric is vacant (from vacancy "until
-- the formal assumption of office by his successor"). Encoded with a single flag for the vacancy. The Gazette proves authorisation;
-- it is not a condition of holding office on the words of s 5 (an inference from the wording).
DECLARE Office IS ONE OF
    `Archbishop`
    `Administrator Apostolic`
    `Vicar Capitular`
    `parish priest`

GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office, `the Archbishopric is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Corporation for the time being` IF
    CONSIDER `the office`
    WHEN `Archbishop` THEN NOT `the Archbishopric is vacant`
    WHEN `Administrator Apostolic` THEN `the Archbishopric is vacant`
    WHEN `Vicar Capitular` THEN `the Archbishopric is vacant`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office, `the appointment is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `authorisation is conclusively proved` IF
        `the appointment is notified in the Gazette`
    AND CONSIDER `the office`
        WHEN `parish priest` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2(4) -- no concurrent holders, and when a power of attorney ends`

-- s 2(4): "There shall not be concurrent holders of any 2 of the offices of Archbishop, Administrator Apostolic or Vicar Capitular and
-- any power of attorney given by any one of them shall cease to be valid when the donor of the power of attorney ceases to administer
-- the affairs of the diocese."
--
-- "Concurrent holders of any 2 of the offices" is read as: at most one of the three offices is filled at any one time (an inference;
-- the words could also be read as one person holding two offices, which this reading also forbids).
GIVEN `an Archbishop is in office` IS A BOOLEAN, `an Administrator Apostolic is in office` IS A BOOLEAN, `a Vicar Capitular is in office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there are concurrent holders` IF
        (`an Archbishop is in office` AND `an Administrator Apostolic is in office`)
    OR  (`an Archbishop is in office` AND `a Vicar Capitular is in office`)
    OR  (`an Administrator Apostolic is in office` AND `a Vicar Capitular is in office`)

GIVEN `the donor still administers the affairs of the diocese` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power of attorney is still valid` IF
    `the donor still administers the affairs of the diocese`

§§ `2(1) and 2(2) -- what the Corporation may do`

-- s 2(1): the Corporation shall "be capable of acquiring, holding and disposing of movable and immovable property, of suing and being
-- sued and of performing all such acts and things as bodies corporate may lawfully perform".
-- s 2(2): "The seal, which may consist of a rubber stamp, may from time to time be broken, changed, altered and made anew as to the
-- Corporation seems fit."
--
-- Unlike the Bishop of Singapore Ordinance 1911 (as quoted in that Ordinance's naive row), the capacity to sue and be sued is not tied to property, and there is a general
-- capacity to do what bodies corporate may lawfully do.
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `acquire property`
    `hold property`
    `sell or otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue`
    `be sued`
    `use a rubber stamp as its seal`
    `change its seal`
    `do an act a body corporate may lawfully perform`
    `do an act no body corporate may lawfully perform`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act makes the Corporation capable to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `do an act no body corporate may lawfully perform` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 -- property of the Titular Roman Catholic Bishop of Malacca`

-- s 3: "All movable and immovable properties of every description situate in Singapore which immediately before 12 December 1975 were
-- vested in the Titular Roman Catholic Bishop of Malacca (referred to in this Act as the former Corporation) whether with or without
-- the name of the ecclesiastic for the time being holding office, and whether with or without the addition of the words 'resident in
-- the Straits Settlements', is hereby vested in the Corporation for the respective estates and interests for which the same is held."
--
-- Movable property is swept in as well as land. Property outside Singapore (for instance in Malacca or Johore, which the preamble says
-- were once in the same Archdiocese) is not. The form of the name on the title makes no difference.
DECLARE Holding HAS
    `is situate in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was vested in the former Corporation immediately before 12 December 1975` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is movable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the title names the individual bishop` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the title adds resident in the Straits Settlements` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 vests it in the Corporation` IF
        `the holding`'s `is situate in Singapore`
    AND `the holding`'s `was vested in the former Corporation immediately before 12 December 1975`

§§ `4 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 4(1): instruments requiring the seal "shall be sealed with the seal of the Corporation in the presence of the Roman Catholic
-- Archbishop of Singapore for the time being or when the Archbishopric is vacant in the presence of the Administrator Apostolic or of
-- the Vicar Capitular ..., as the case may be, or the attorney of any one of them duly authorised by a power of attorney deposited
-- pursuant to section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, and shall also be signed by the Archbishop for the time
-- being or by the Administrator Apostolic or Vicar Capitular, as the case may be, or the attorney of any one of them so authorised."
-- s 4(2): "Such signing shall be sufficient evidence that the seal was duly and properly affixed and that the seal is the lawful seal
-- of the Corporation."
--
-- The Archbishop qualifies only while the see is filled, and the Administrator Apostolic or Vicar Capitular only while it is vacant.
-- An attorney qualifies only if the power was deposited AND (s 2(4)) the donor still administers the diocese. The witness and the
-- signer need not be the same person on the words of s 4(1); that reading is encoded.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Archbishop`
    `the Administrator Apostolic`
    `the Vicar Capitular`
    `an attorney under a deposited power whose donor still administers`
    `an attorney under a deposited power whose donor has ceased to administer`
    `an attorney whose power of attorney is not deposited`
    `a parish priest with no power of attorney`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `the Archbishopric is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer, `the see is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may witness and sign for the Corporation` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the Archbishop` THEN NOT `the see is vacant`
    WHEN `the Administrator Apostolic` THEN `the see is vacant`
    WHEN `the Vicar Capitular` THEN `the see is vacant`
    WHEN `an attorney under a deposited power whose donor still administers` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 4 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may witness and sign for the Corporation` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`) (`the instrument`'s `the Archbishopric is vacant`)
    AND `may witness and sign for the Corporation` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`) (`the instrument`'s `the Archbishopric is vacant`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence the seal was duly affixed` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may witness and sign for the Corporation` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`) (`the instrument`'s `the Archbishopric is vacant`)

§§ `6 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 6: "Nothing in this Act shall affect the rights of the President or of any body politic or corporate or of any other person except
-- such as are mentioned in this Act and those claiming by, from or under them."
GIVEN `is mentioned in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act may affect their rights` IF
    `is mentioned in the Act` OR `claims by, from or under a person mentioned`

§§ `7 -- agreements, staff, unfinished business and liabilities of the former Corporation`

-- s 7(1): "every agreement, whether in writing or not, to which the former Corporation was a party immediately before 12 December 1975,
-- and whether or not of such nature that the rights and liabilities thereunder could be assigned, shall have effect as from that date
-- as if (a) the Corporation had been a party to such an agreement; and (b) [references to the former Corporation read as references to
-- the Corporation]".
-- s 7(2): "The appointment of any officer or employee of the former Corporation subsisting immediately before 12 December 1975 shall,
-- if that officer or employee so agrees, be deemed to be made by the Corporation, and for the purpose of determining the rate of
-- pension and gratuities on retirement the service ... shall be regarded as continuous from the time he was appointed by the former
-- Corporation."
-- s 7(3): anything "commenced under the authority of the former Corporation before 12 December 1975 ... may be carried on and completed
-- under the authority of the Corporation".
-- s 7(4): "All rights, obligations and liabilities which immediately before 12 December 1975 were vested in or incurred by the former
-- Corporation shall pass by succession to the Corporation".
--
-- Writing and assignability make no difference under s 7(1). The employee's consent is a condition under s 7(2). s 7(1) is "subject to
-- subsection (2)", so an employment agreement is taken under s 7(2), not s 7(1) (an inference from those words).
GIVEN `the former Corporation was a party immediately before 12 December 1975` IS A BOOLEAN, `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `the rights could be assigned` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is an appointment of an officer or employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement has effect as if the Corporation were a party` IF
        `the former Corporation was a party immediately before 12 December 1975`
    AND (NOT `it is an appointment of an officer or employee`)

GIVEN `the appointment subsisted immediately before 12 December 1975` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer or employee agrees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment is deemed made by the Corporation` IF
    `the appointment subsisted immediately before 12 December 1975` AND `the officer or employee agrees`

GIVEN `the appointment subsisted immediately before 12 December 1975` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer or employee agrees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `service counts as continuous for pension and gratuity` IF
    `the appointment is deemed made by the Corporation` `the appointment subsisted immediately before 12 December 1975` `the officer or employee agrees`

GIVEN `commenced under the former Corporation's authority before 12 December 1975` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be carried on and completed under the Corporation` IF
    `commenced under the former Corporation's authority before 12 December 1975`

GIVEN `vested in or incurred by the former Corporation immediately before 12 December 1975` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `passes by succession to the Corporation` IF
    `vested in or incurred by the former Corporation immediately before 12 December 1975`
